! **Eight atoms and a cell under 500 kbar.** The conventional cubic cell of
! diamond silicon -- a supercell of the primitive one, which P28a established is
! a regime rather than a size -- compressed by an applied pressure and relaxed
! back with `calculation = 'vc-relax'`.
!
! What it adds over the two-atom arsenic of QE's own `pw_vc-relax` cases is
! everything that scales with the cell: eight atoms whose forces and nine cell
! coordinates share one Hessian, a structure factor that vanishes *exactly* at
! the G-vectors the cubic cell's exact fractions kill (P28a's `abs` trap, whose
! consumer here is the stress rather than the second derivative), and a
! neighbour list large enough that an image lost to compression is a real term
! rather than an erfc tail below the comparison floor.
!
! `celldm(1) = 10.20` is silicon's zero-pressure lattice constant to within
! what this functional relaxes it to (10.19 with `Si.pz-vbc`), so the whole of
! the trajectory is the response to the pressure: `pw.x` takes it to 9.252 bohr,
! a 25% compression. Diamond silicon is metastable against beta-tin above ~110
! kbar and this run does not know that -- which is fine, because what is being
! compared is two codes on one well-defined energy surface, not a phase diagram.
!
! Cubic symmetry survives the trajectory, so the relaxed cell must still be
! cubic. Nothing imposes it -- `cell_dofree` is `'all'`, so every entry of `h`
! is free to move -- which makes the off-diagonal entries returning to zero a
! check on the symmetrised stress that shares nothing with `pw.x`.
 &control
    calculation = 'vc-relax'
    tprnfor = .true.
    tstress = .true.
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 1
    celldm(1) = 10.20
    nat = 8
    ntyp = 1
    ecutwfc = 24.0
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
 &ions
 /
 &cell
    cell_dynamics = 'bfgs'
    press = 500.0
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si  28.086  Si.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS crystal
 Si 0.00 0.00 0.00
 Si 0.00 0.50 0.50
 Si 0.50 0.00 0.50
 Si 0.50 0.50 0.00
 Si 0.25 0.25 0.25
 Si 0.25 0.75 0.75
 Si 0.75 0.25 0.75
 Si 0.75 0.75 0.25
K_POINTS automatic
 4 4 4 0 0 0
